 Depth: Make planting holes about 5 cm deep [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth], or avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "- Plant Spacing: Use a row-to-row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing], or 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants within the rows [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "- Plant after the rains are well established to avoid prolonged dry spells [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "A rainfall record is attached for the officer's reference.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No rainfall record"}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset, so AgriReach does not say whether the guides' condition is met; the officer decides.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages imply"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'Choose which planting window to follow.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No choice", "'Choose which planting depth to follow.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No choice", "'Choose which plant spacing to follow.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No choice"], "figures_checked": 11, "sentences_checked": 7, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Plant soybean in the northern region between mid-June and late July [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window], or between mid-June and mid-July [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Choose which planting window to follow.", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No choice"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Do not plant too early before the rains are well established [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Make planting holes about 5 cm deep [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth], or avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "Choose which planting depth to follow.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No choice"}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "Use a row to row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing], or a spacing of 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants within the rows [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 7, "sentence": "Choose which plant spacing to follow.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No choice"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "Plant soybean in the northern region between mid-June and late July [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window], or between mid-June and mid-July [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window]. Choose which planting window to follow. Do not plant too early before the rains are well established [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture]. Make planting holes about 5 cm deep [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth], or avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth]. Choose which planting depth to follow. Use a row to row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing], or a spacing of 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants within the rows [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing]. Choose which plant spacing to follow."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Soybean planting in the northern region should be done between mid-June and late July based on the onset of the rains and the variety.\" [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window]\n- \"Do not plant too early before the rains are well established as a prolonged dry spell after planting may cause the plants to die.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture]\n- \"To achieve the desired spacing, make planting holes that are about 5 cm deep at a spacing of 15 cm between holes.\" [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth]\n- \"The best planting time for soyabean is between mid-June to mid-July with the rains likely well established.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window]\n- \"The recommended plant spacing for soybean in northern Ghana is a row to row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row.\" [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing]\n- \"This will allow the recommended spacing of 50 cm between rows (roughly the length of two footprints) and 10 cm between plants within the rows (roughly the length from the base of your thumb to the top of your index finger) to be applied and to achieve the required plant population.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing]\n- \"Avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) as this may result in loss of seed vigor and poor germination or failure to germinate.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth]\n- \"Rainfall record (Open-Meteo (model-based estimate, forecast API past days); CC BY 4.0) for Wa district (point: Wa (district capital), 10.0607, -2.5019), 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24: 17 of 30 days with at least 1 mm; total 149.9 mm. Retrieved 2026-10-25T19:49:20+00:00. This is a model estimate for one point in the district, not a rain gauge reading; estimates can differ a lot from a local gauge and from other providers. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset; AgriReach does not say whether onset has been reached. The officer decides.\" [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:wa:2026-10-25]\nNote: Sources give different figures for planting window; officer should choose.\nNote: Sources give different figures for planting depth; officer should choose.\nNote: Sources give different figures for plant spacing; officer should choose.\nNote: A rainfall record is attached for the officer. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset, so AgriReach does not say whether the guides' condition is met; the officer decides.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between mid-June and late July; IITA, northern region: between mid-June to mid-July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) District Wa taken from the question text.\nNote: (officer only) Rainfall record [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:wa:2026-10-25] for Wa, 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24: 17 rain days (at least 1 mm), 149.9 mm in total, 0 days missing (Open-Meteo (model-based estimate, forecast API past days)). This is a model estimate for one point in the district, not a rain gauge reading; estimates can differ a lot from a local gauge and from other providers. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset; AgriReach does not say whether onset has been reached. The officer decides.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3103, "completion_tokens": 562}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 2995, "completion_tokens": 289}}, "cost_usd": 0.001499}}
