, "sentence": "- **Plant Spacing:** Sources disagree.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Wrong passage"}, {"n": 9, "sentence": "[APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth] says to space 15 cm between holes.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 10, "sentence": "[APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing] says to space 50 cm between rows and 15 cm between plants in a row.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 11, "sentence": "[IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing] says to space 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants in a row.", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 12, "sentence": "- **Rainfall Record:** From 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24, Tamale had 15 of 30 days with at least 1 mm of rain, totaling 137.2 mm [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:tamale:2026-10-25].", "cited": ["RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:tamale:2026-10-25"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "**Soybean Planting Advice for Tamale**\n\n- **Planting Window:** Sources disagree. [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window] says to plant between mid-June and late July. [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window] says to plant between mid-June to mid-July. Choose one.\n- **Planting Depth:** Sources disagree. [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth] says to plant 5 cm deep. [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth] says to plant 3 cm deep, not deeper than 5 cm. Choose one.\n- **Plant Spacing:** Sources disagree. [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth] says to space 15 cm between holes. [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing] says to space 50 cm between rows and 15 cm between plants in a row. [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing] says to space 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants in a row. Choose one.\n- **Rainfall Record:** From 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24, Tamale had 15 of 30 days with at least 1 mm of rain, totaling 137.2 mm [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:tamale:2026-10-25]."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Soybean planting in the northern region should be done between mid-June and late July based on the onset of the rains and the variety.\" [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window]\n- \"Do not plant too early before the rains are well established as a prolonged dry spell after planting may cause the plants to die.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture]\n- \"To achieve the desired spacing, make planting holes that are about 5 cm deep at a spacing of 15 cm between holes.\" [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth]\n- \"The best planting time for soyabean is between mid-June to mid-July with the rains likely well established.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window]\n- \"The recommended plant spacing for soybean in northern Ghana is a row to row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row.\" [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing]\n- \"This will allow the recommended spacing of 50 cm between rows (roughly the length of two footprints) and 10 cm between plants within the rows (roughly the length from the base of your thumb to the top of your index finger) to be applied and to achieve the required plant population.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing]\n- \"Avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) as this may result in loss of seed vigor and poor germination or failure to germinate.\" [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth]\n- \"Rainfall record (Open-Meteo (model-based estimate, forecast API past days); CC BY 4.0) for Tamale district (point: Tamale (district capital), 9.4008, -0.8393), 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24: 15 of 30 days with at least 1 mm; total 137.2 mm. Retrieved 2026-10-25T17:39:09+00:00. This is a model estimate for one point in the district, not a rain gauge reading; estimates can differ a lot from a local gauge and from other providers. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset; AgriReach does not say whether onset has been reached. The officer decides.\" [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:tamale:2026-10-25]\nNote: Sources give different figures for planting window; officer should choose.\nNote: Sources give different figures for planting depth; officer should choose.\nNote: Sources give different figures for plant spacing; officer should choose.\nNote: A rainfall record is attached for the officer. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset, so AgriReach does not say whether the guides' condition is met; the officer decides.\nNote: The farmer wrote in Twi. This draft is in English for the officer, who must reply in Twi.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between mid-June and late July; IITA, northern region: between mid-June to mid-July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) District Tamale taken from the question text.\nNote: (officer only) Rainfall record [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:tamale:2026-10-25] for Tamale, 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24: 15 rain days (at least 1 mm), 137.2 mm in total, 0 days missing (Open-Meteo (model-based estimate, forecast API past days)). This is a model estimate for one point in the district, not a rain gauge reading; estimates can differ a lot from a local gauge and from other providers. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset; AgriReach does not say whether onset has been reached. The officer decides.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3781, "completion_tokens": 748}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3645, "completion_tokens": 512}}, "cost_usd": 0.001222}}
